---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`Privacy notes for ${site.title}. This is not legal advice.`}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What this site does</h2>
    <p>
      The pages are built ahead of time from Markdown files. There is no account, no sign-in, and no database. The
      site does not include an analytics script or an advertising script.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      When GitHub Pages is turned on, GitHub serves the built files. This page does not describe GitHub’s own privacy
      terms. Read those on GitHub, and change this section if the files are hosted somewhere else.
    </p>
    <h2>Public repository</h2>
    <p>
      If the GitHub repository is public, the Markdown files, drafts, and media are public even when
      <code>draft: true</code> keeps a tutorial off the built site. Do not commit secrets or private pictures.
    </p>
    <h2>YouTube</h2>
    <p>
      A tutorial loads a player from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> only when that tutorial’s file includes a
      video link. YouTube’s policies apply to that player. Delete the link to remove the player.
    </p>
    <h2>Ads</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ads.enabled</code> is {site.ads.enabled ? 'true' : 'false'}. While it is false, no ad slot is shown and no
      publisher ID is included. This site does not claim approval from any ad network.
    </p>
    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>
      The archive filter runs in the visitor’s browser on a list built with the site. It is not sent to a search
      company by this site.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
